    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event for owner creation, alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`): an immutable `record` carrying `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel}` plus the `event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"` discriminator, with a `toJson()` renderer (fixed key order, proper string escaping).\n\nTwo design points from the spec:\n- **Monotonic `seq`** \u2014 a static `AtomicLong` in `AuditOwnerCreated`, incremented once per successful create, so the sequence increases across all creates.\n- **Future-proof primary identifier** \u2014 the event's identifier value is sourced through a single private `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` method that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. Its Javadoc states that when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, changing that one line makes the event carry the memberId instead \u2014 the rest of the pipeline is untouched. This is exactly what the test's doc comment anticipates (\"later checkpoints prove the event switched to the memberId\").\n\n**Edited** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`: after the existing `audit.info(...)` line, it now emits `audit.info(OwnerCreatedEvent.of(SEQ.incrementAndGet(), owner).toJson())` on the same `AUDIT` logger.\n\nThe emitted line looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes (it asserts one AUDIT line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode), and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green.",
